es"]},{"convention":"Positive functionals are real-linear functionals on real-valued C_c(X); the bounded complex result is separately about C_0(X;C).","fixed_by":"def-positive-linear-functional-on-c-c","matters_for":["thm-rmk-positive-functional-is-integration-against-its-representing-measure","thm-rmk-uniqueness-among-radon-measures","thm-bounded-c-zero-functionals-are-regular-complex-measure-integrals"]},{"convention":"The ordinal club-set arguments explicitly assume AC_omega.","fixed_by":"thm-dieudonne-club-set-function-is-a-borel-measure","matters_for":["lem-continuous-functions-on-omega-one-plus-one-are-eventually-constant","lem-dieudonne-measure-and-top-dirac-agree-on-continuous-functions","fs-every-borel-measure-on-an-lch-space-is-radon","fs-rmk-representing-measure-is-unique-among-all-borel-measures"]},{"convention":"Convergence in probability uses P(|X_n-X|>epsilon)→0 for every epsilon>0; distributional convergence is CDF convergence at continuity points of the limit CDF.","fixed_by":"def-convergence-in-probability","matters_for":["thm-convergence-in-probability-implies-convergence-in-distribution","thm-convergence-in-distribution-to-a-constant-is-convergence-in-probability","thm-slutsky-for-real-random-variables","thm-probability-convergence-is-metrized-by-d-zero"]},{"convention":"L^p convergence is convergence of almost-everywhere equivalence classes; p may equal infinity in the definition, but the finite-p implications state their own range.","fixed_by":"def-convergence-in-lp-for-random-variables","matters_for":["thm-lp-convergence-implies-convergence-in-probability","thm-lq-convergence-implies-lp-convergence-on-a-probability-space","thm-dominated-convergence-in-lp","cex-lp-convergence-need-not-imply-almost-sure-convergence"]},{"convention":"A Hadamard-lacunary sequence is strictly increasing, positive-integer valued, indexed from 1, and has one fixed ratio q>1.","fixed_by":"def-hadamard-lacunary-sequence-and-lacunary-trigonometric-series","matters_for":["lem-hadamard-gaps-bound-additive-representations","thm-lacunary-lp-norm-equivalence","lem-riesz-product-for-a-hadamard-lacunary-set","thm-hadamard-lacunary-sets-are-sidon"]},{"convention":"A Sidon set E⊂Z is defined by a uniform l^1-to-supremum-norm inequality for finitely supported coefficient families on E.","fixed_by":"def-sidon-set-in-the-integer-dual","matters_for":["thm-hadamard-lacunary-sets-are-sidon","cor-fourier-series-supported-on-a-sidon-set-and-continuous-has-ell-one-coefficients","cex-the-integers-are-not-a-sidon-set"]}],"load_bearing":[{"id":"lem-finite-lch-partition-of-unity-near-a-compact-set","statement":"Let X be locally compact Hausdorff, let K⊂X be compact, and let U_1,...,U_n be open sets covering K. Then there are nonnegative φ_i∈C_c(X) with supp φ_i⊂U_i such that Σ_iφ_i=1 on an open neighbourhood of K.","used_by":["thm-rmk-functional-outer-content-is-an-outer-measure","thm-rmk-positive-functional-is-integration-against-its-representing-measure","thm-lusin-theorem-for-radon-measures"]},{"id":"thm-rmk-positive-functional-is-integration-against-its-representing-measure","statement":"Let X be LCH and let Λ:C_c(X;R)→R be positive. The Radon measure μ constructed above satisfies Λ(f)=∫_X f dμ for every f∈C_c(X;R).","used_by":["thm-rmk-uniqueness-among-radon-measures","lem-positive-c-zero-functionals-have-finite-regular-representing-measures","ex-riemann-integral-functional-is-represented-by-interval-lebesgue-measure","ex-point-evaluation-functional-is-represented-by-a-dirac-measure","ex-locally-integrable-density-functional-is-represented-by-g-dlambda","ex-lebesgue-stieltjes-functional-is-represented-by-its-stieltjes-measure","ex-counting-functional-on-a-discrete-lch-space"]},{"id":"def-convergence-in-probability","statement":"For real random variables (X_n) and X on one probability space, X_n→X in probability when, for every ε>0, P(|X_n-X|>ε)→0.","used_by":["thm-limits-in-probability-are-unique-almost-surely","thm-almost-sure-convergence-implies-convergence-in-probability","thm-lp-convergence-implies-convergence-in-probability","thm-convergence-in-probability-implies-convergence-in-distribution","thm-almost-sure-subsequence-from-convergence-in-probability","thm-probability-convergence-is-metrized-by-d-zero","thm-slutsky-for-real-random-variables"]},{"id":"thm-lacunary-lp-norm-equivalence","statement":"For q>1 and 0<p<∞, constants c_{p,q},C_{p,q}>0 make every finite q-Hadamard-lacunary sum satisfy c_{p,q}(Σ|a_j|²)^{1/2}≤||f||_{L^p(T)}≤C_{p,q}(Σ|a_j|²)^{1/2}.","used_by":["cor-lacunary-series-lp-membership-is-coefficient-ell-two"]},{"id":"lem-riesz-product-for-a-hadamard-lacunary-set","statement":"For each ratio-three residue class of a finite positive Hadamard-lacunary set, the stated Riesz product is nonnegative, has integral 1, and has Fourier coefficient \\widehat P_ν(-λ)=\\overline{ε_λ}/2.","used_by":["thm-hadamard-lacunary-sets-are-sidon","ex-riesz-product-for-three-powers-of-three"]}],"published_dependencies":[{"id":"thm-urysohn-lemma","used_for":"The LCH cutoff construction.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-caratheodory-outer-measure-theorem","used_for":"The measurable-set sigma-algebra and induced measure in the RMK construction.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-lebesgue-outer-regularity-for-arbitrary-subsets","used_for":"The claimed outer regularity of Lebesgue measure.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-lebesgue-inner-regularity-by-closed-and-compact-sets","used_for":"The claimed compact inner regularity of Lebesgue measure.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-countable-subsets-of-omega-one-are-bounded","used_for":"The AC_omega ordinal and club arguments.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-ordinal-spaces-and-compactness","used_for":"Compactness of [0,omega_1].","opened":true},{"id":"def-probability-measure","used_for":"Probability-space normalization.","opened":true},{"id":"def-convergence-in-measure","used_for":"Identification with probability convergence and Vitali.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-dominated-convergence","used_for":"Almos